<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Nowhere in this article have I read anything in particular that indicates anomalous activity.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What happened to Harolds was quite anomalous. Even if he was slowly devoured by the insects, he only move after making physical contact with another human. That's weird.</p>
<p>And also these,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4676 only affects individuals who are alone at the time of onset, and preferentially targets those at least 55 meters from any other human being or human habitation1.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Most of the victims are found at a very specific location/distance and,</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4676 events have no known maximum duration, ending only upon nullification via physical contact with another human being or the death of the victim.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Although not explicitly stated, the Foundation has witnessed these people only starting to move after making physical contact with another human.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>You know what they say about hearing hoofbeats and leaping straight to thinking about zebras</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Not really. When I hear hoofbeats, I just think &quot;Hmm, could it be a cow or a horse, better check it out&quot;. Sometimes, you can recognize who the hoofbeats belong to because horses are rhythmic and cows are usually slow and heavy.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Suspension of disbelief shattered by Occam's razor.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Since we have inherently different views on things, I can't do anything about this.</p>
<p>Thanks for reading it though.</p>
